'''''Prunus glandulosa''''', called '''Chinese bush cherry''', '''Chinese plum''', and '''dwarf flowering almond''', is a species of shrub tree native to China and long present in Japan. It is commonly used as an ornamental tree and for [[cut flowers]].<ref name="grin">{{GRIN | accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref><ref name="tamu">{{cite web |url=http://aggie-horticulture.tamu.edu/newsletters/hortupdate/hortupdate_archives/1995-1997/HUFEB96.pdf|title=Flowering almond, ''Prunus glandulosa'' |work=Horticulture Update |publisher=Texas A&M University|date=February 1996 |accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref>

It has white or pink flowers - single or double varies with cultivar - that bloom in Spring. Fruits are dark red.<ref name="urbana">{{cite web|url=http://urbanext.illinois.edu/ShrubSelector/detail_plant.cfm?PlantID=364|title= Dwarf Flowering Almond Prunus glandulosa |publisher=University of Illinois - Urbana|accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref> Its height is about {{convert|1.5|m|ft|sp=us}} and prefers rocky slopes with plenty of sun. Leaves are alternating, pointy, and light green.<ref name="conn">{{cite web|url=http://www.hort.uconn.edu/plants/detail.php?pid=350|title= Prunus glandulosa |publisher=University of Connecticut|accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref><ref name="pfaf">{{cite web|url=http://www.pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Prunus+glandulosa|title=Prunus glandulosa - Thunb.|publisher=Plants For a Future|accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref> It is drought tolerant.<ref name="ncsu">{{cite web|url=http://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/all/prunus-glandulosa/|title= Dwarf Flowering Almond Prunus glandulosa |publisher=North Carolina State University|accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref> It is susceptible to mice as well as these diseases: [[fire blight]], [[leaf spot]], [[die back]], [[leaf curl]], [[powdery mildew]], [[root rot]], and [[Armillaria|honey fungus]].<ref name="mobon">{{cite web|url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=286615&isprofile=0&#AllImages|title= Prunus glandulosa |publisher=Missouri Botanical Garden|accessdate=November 11, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?kempercode=d136|title=Prunus glandulosa 'Sinensis' - Plant Finder}}</ref>

Cultivars include: 'Alba' - (single white flowers), 'Alba Plena' (also 'Alboplena') - (double white flowers), 'Lawrence' - (single white-pink flowers), 'Rosea Plena' (also 'Sinensis') - (double pink flowers).<ref name="conn" />

